WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.500
What is up everyone! Welcome to the premiere episode of A Cast About Everything.

00:05.500 --> 00:11.000
I’m your host, Noah Burr, broadcasting live from the living room couch,

00:11.000 --> 00:16.200
and today I am telling you the absolute craziest story of my tech crisis.

00:16.200 --> 00:21.000
So right now, I am currently trapped at home fighting off a massive case of strep throat.

00:21.000 --> 00:26.500
Swallowing feels like literal razor blades and my perfect attendance streak at school is completely dead.

00:26.500 --> 00:31.500
So my current survival strategy is sitting here, wrapped in a blanket like a burrito,

00:31.500 --> 00:35.000
taking tiny sips of ice water, and trying to read a normal style website.

00:35.000 --> 00:40.000
And then, the exact millisecond my mouse hits the screen canvas—BOOM.

00:40.000 --> 00:44.200
A broken, sketchy ad script completely hijacks my browser tab.

00:44.200 --> 00:49.000
It skips three redirect loops, and dumps me straight onto an adult domain.

00:49.000 --> 00:53.000
I panicked so hard I smashed the back button within a split second to close the window,

00:53.000 --> 00:56.500
but the damage was done. It was officially burned into the history logs.

00:56.500 --> 01:01.000
Now, standard protocol is simple: open settings, click clear history, crisis averted.

01:01.000 --> 01:05.800
Except Apple's Screen Time parental controls are fully locked down on my device.

01:05.800 --> 01:09.500
The delete button is completely frozen. I can’t clear the cache at all.

01:09.500 --> 01:13.500
Honestly? When you’re dealing with a glitchy internet ad popup redirect,

01:13.500 --> 01:17.000
trying to write custom code workarounds to bypass Apple's walls is a waste of time.

01:17.000 --> 01:21.500
The only real move is to just be completely candid. It got out in the open,

01:21.500 --> 01:25.500
the situation was completely understood, and it turned out to be a total non-issue.

01:25.500 --> 01:30.000
And that is how a boring Wednesday sick day turned into a full-blown security extraction mission.

01:30.000 --> 01:34.500
The history is safe, the dashboard is secure, and A Cast About Everything is officially live.

01:34.500 --> 01:39.000
Head over to noahburr.org to refresh my live traffic analytics counters!

01:39.000 --> 01:42.000
And I will catch you guys on the next transmission. Peace out!
